<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Kehl</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Kehl is a town in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baden-wurttemberg">Baden-Württemberg</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a>, on the east bank of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rhine">Rhine</a> opposite Strasbourg, to which it is linked by bridges and a tram line. For centuries it guarded the Rhine crossing and was fortified and fought over in the wars between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> and the Empire. It belonged to the counts of Hanau-Lichtenberg and later to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baden">Baden</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/kehl.jpg" alt="Kehl" width="320" height="180" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Oliver Griebl · CC BY 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Trambr%C3%BCcke_(220033777).jpeg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
